          %h4#ModLayerNonabelianChargedParticle Nonabelian charged particle and Wilson loops
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
            which describes the gauge interaction of a single nonabelian charged particle – a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loop"} Wilson loop
            – turns out to be equivalent to what in mathematics is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+method"} orbit method
            %em
              %a{:href => "#GaugeAndGravityWilsonLoops"} Semantics layer – Nonabelian charged particle and Wilson loops
            we then show how all this is naturally understood from a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+Lagrangian"} extended Lagrangian
            which is induced by a regular
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+orbit"} coadjoint orbit
          %p
            A useful review of the following is also in (
            %a{:href => "#Beasley"}> Beasley, section 4
            ).
          %h5#the_group_and_its_lie_algebra The group and its Lie algebra
          %p
            Throughout, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+group"} semisimple
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+group"} compact
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            we write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle -,-\rangle : \mathfrak{g} \otimes \mathfrak{g} \to \mathbb{R}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Since this is non-degenerate, we may equivalently think of this as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathfrak{g} \simeq \mathfrak{g}^*
          %p
            that identifies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            underlying the Lie algebra with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} dual vector space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
          %h5#the_coadjoint_orbit_and_the_coset_space_flag_manifold The coadjoint orbit and the coset space/ flag manifold
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+orbits"} coadjoint orbits
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and their relation to the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+manifolds"} flag manifolds
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p Write
          %ol
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \hookrightarrow G
              inclusion of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal torus
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔱
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{t} \hookrightarrow \mathfrak{g}
            the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+subalgebra"} Cartan subalgebra
          %p
            In all of the following we consider an element
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle\lambda,-\rangle \in \mathfrak{g}^*
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle\lambda,-\rangle \in \mathfrak{g}^*
              write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi λ
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O}_\lambda \hookrightarrow \mathfrak{g}^*
            %p
              for its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+orbit"} coadjoint orbit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi λ
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ad
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O}_{\lambda} = \{ Ad_g^*(\langle\lambda,-\rangle) \in \mathfrak{g}^* | g \in G \}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi λ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\lambda \hookrightarrow G
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizer subgroup
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \lambda,-\rangle
              under the coadjoint action.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p There is an equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi λ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G/G_\lambda \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \mathcal{O}_\lambda
            %p given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi λ
                    %mo ↦
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ad
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g G_\lambda \mapsto Ad_g^* \langle\lambda,-\rangle
                    \\,.
          #RegularElement.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              An element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle\lambda,-\rangle \in \mathfrak{g}^*
              is
              %strong regular
              if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+action"} coadjoint action
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizer subgroup
              coincides with the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal torus
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mi λ
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\lambda \simeq T
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For generic values of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              it is regular. The element in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
              farthest from regularity is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda = 0
              for which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi λ
                    %mo =
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\lambda = G
              instead.
          %h5#the_symplectic_form The symplectic form
          %p
            We describe a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
            on the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+orbit"} coadjoint orbit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset"} coset
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi λ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi λ
