          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_8 Remark
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
              the diagram in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheTwistedHolonomyMapOnTwistedUnitaryBundles"}
              says in particular that forming traced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
              of twisted unitary bundles constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
              of twisted unitary connection on the circle which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi π
                    %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi dd
                        %mo ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(2 \pi i \int_{S^1} [S^1, \widehat\mathbf{dd}_n])
              of the universal differential
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dixmier-Douady+class"} Dixmier-Douady class
          %p
            It follows that on the moduli space of the open string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            of prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheTypeIIOpenStringSigmaModelModuliStackOfFields"}
            above there are two
            = succeed "-valued" do
